[Debug] ----- Vuln Cause Analysis -----
The potential vulnerability lies in the insufficient entropy of the generated salts. The code specifies that salts should be of the same length as the output hash, but it doesn't explicitly define a minimum length or a method to ensure sufficient randomness. If the generated salts are too short or predictable, it could weaken the security of the password hashing process, making it more susceptible to rainbow table attacks or other precomputation-based cryptanalytic techniques. This lack of robust salt generation can compromise the overall security of the stored password hashes.

